§ `Article 111 and Article 113: does the group General apply on the date asked?`
-- The group General holds every provision that no point of Article 113 dates separately, among them Articles 111 to 113 themselves: it applies from 2 August 2026 (Art 113, second paragraph).
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1657 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2199 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
@ref Art 113 first and second paragraphs: the group General (Articles 111 to 113 and every provision no point of Article 113 dates) (src:1656-1657) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198-2199)
-- A legacy high-risk AI system saved by Article 111(2) is a separate question (Under Article 111(2), first sentence).
@export Under Article 111, as a provider of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 111, as a provider of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat provider from part P1 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P1-seat-provider: THE SEAT LAYER of part P1 (Articles 5 to 7, Annexes I, II, III) for a provider of an AI system.
-- Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. A thin layer over the P1 layer-1 modules: every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a date, a number, or one of the
-- Regulation's own choices), builds nothing new, and calls the layer-1 rule; no rule is restated here. Nothing in this file is law; the consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.
-- Fork F-5-3-defined-terms: where a layer-1 function takes a term of Article 3 as one yes/no input, the question asks the facts that the keel's Article 3 function takes, as plain inputs, and works the term
-- out in a WHERE by calling that function (aia-definitions.l4). The AI system is taken to be an AI system within Article 3(1) (the keel's first input is passed TRUE). The terms left as plain facts are in fork F-5-3-terms-left-as-facts.
-- Commencement is IN (assumed, not ruled): every answer is asked for a date, and a provision that does not yet apply on that date answers NOTHING (not covered), never JUST FALSE.
-- Fork F-seat-act: the role fixes the act asked about under Article 5(1): the placing on the market or the putting into service (the caller says which).
-- How to read an answer: JUST TRUE the text says yes to the question the name asks; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words (a carve-out, an 'only', a failed 'where'); NOTHING not covered
-- (the provision does not apply on that date, or the facts leave an element of the provision unmet or outside its words). NOTES.md, 'Reading a result', says which is which.
-- ASSUMED ROLE: the person asking holds this role; the role question is its own question. The AI system is taken to be an AI system within Article 3(1): the seat does not restate Article 3.

§ `Under Article 5: who is asking`

§§ `The role`

@export Under Article 5, as a provider of an AI system, am I a provider within the meaning of Article 3(3)?
GIVEN `the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you develop an AI system or a general-purpose AI model?
      `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed for you?
      `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you place that system or model on the market, or put the AI system into service?
      `the party does so under its own name or trademark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do so under your own name or trademark?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5, as a provider of an AI system, am I a provider within the meaning of Article 3(3)` IS
    `Art 3(3) the party is a provider` `the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed` `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service` `the party does so under its own name or trademark`

