@export Under Article 13(1), as a provider of an AI system, in the second sentence, is an appropriate type and degree of transparency ensured in my high-risk AI system with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `an appropriate type and degree of transparency is ensured with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that an appropriate type and degree of transparency is ensured with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 13(1), as a provider of an AI system, in the second sentence, is an appropriate type and degree of transparency ensured in my high-risk AI system with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3` IS
    `Art 13(1) second sentence an appropriate type and degree of transparency is ensured with a view to compliance with the obligations of the provider and deployer` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `an appropriate type and degree of transparency is ensured with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 13(2), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system accompanied by instructions for use, in an appropriate digital format or otherwise, that include concise, complete, correct and clear information that is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the high-risk AI system is accompanied by instructions for use in an appropriate digital format or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the high-risk AI system is accompanied by instructions for use in an appropriate digital format or otherwise?
      `the instructions for use include concise, complete, correct and clear information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the instructions for use include concise, complete, correct and clear information?
      `the information is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the information is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 13(2), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system accompanied by instructions for use, in an appropriate digital format or otherwise, that include concise, complete, correct and clear information that is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers` IS
    `Art 13(2) the high-risk AI system is accompanied by instructions for use that include concise, complete, correct and clear information` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the high-risk AI system is accompanied by instructions for use in an appropriate digital format or otherwise` `the instructions for use include concise, complete, correct and clear information` `the information is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 13(3), as a provider of an AI system, do the instructions for use of my high-risk AI system contain at least the information the paragraph lists?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the instructions for use contain the identity and the contact details of the provider and, where applicable, of its authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the instructions for use contain the identity and the contact details of the provider and, where there is one, of its authorised representative?
      `the instructions for use contain the characteristics, capabilities and limitations of performance of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the instructions for use contain the characteristics, capabilities and limitations of performance of the high-risk AI system?
      `the instructions for use contain its intended purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the instructions for use contain its intended purpose?
      `the instructions for use contain the level of accuracy, including its metrics, robustness and cybersecurity referred to in Article 15 against which the high-risk AI system has been tested and validated and which can be expected, and any known and foreseeable circumstances that may have an impact on that expected level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the instructions for use contain the level of accuracy, including its metrics, robustness and cybersecurity referred to in Article 15 against which the high-risk AI system has been tested and validated and which can be expected, and any known and foreseeable circumstances that may have an impact on that expected level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity?
      `the instructions for use contain any known or foreseeable circumstance, related to the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, which may lead to risks to the health and safety or fundamental rights referred to in Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the instructions for use contain any known or foreseeable circumstance, related to the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, which may lead to risks to the health and safety or fundamental rights referred to in Article 9(2)?
      `the instructions for use contain where applicable, the technical capabilities and characteristics of the high-risk AI system to provide information that is relevant to explain its output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where it is applicable, do the instructions for use contain the technical capabilities and characteristics of the high-risk AI system to provide information that is relevant to explain its output? Answer yes if it is not applicable.
      `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, its performance regarding specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it is appropriate, do the instructions for use contain the performance of the high-risk AI system regarding specific persons or groups of persons on which it is intended to be used? Answer yes if it is not appropriate.
      `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, specifications for the input data, or any other relevant information in terms of the training, validation and testing data sets used, taking into account the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it is appropriate, do the instructions for use contain specifications for the input data, or any other relevant information in terms of the training, validation and testing data sets used, taking into account the intended purpose? Answer yes if it is not appropriate.
      `the instructions for use contain where applicable, information to enable deployers to interpret the output of the high-risk AI system and use it appropriately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where it is applicable, do the instructions for use contain information to enable deployers to interpret the output of the high-risk AI system and use it appropriately? Answer yes if it is not applicable.
      `the instructions for use contain the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance which have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the instructions for use contain the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance which the provider pre-determined at the moment of the initial conformity assessment, if there are any? Answer yes if it is not applicable.
      `the instructions for use contain the human oversight measures referred to in Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of the high-risk AI systems by the deployers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the instructions for use contain the human oversight measures referred to in Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of the high-risk AI systems by the deployers?
      `the instructions for use contain the computational and hardware resources needed, the expected lifetime of the high-risk AI system and any necessary maintenance and care measures, including their frequency, to ensure the proper functioning of that AI system, including as regards software updates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the instructions for use contain the computational and hardware resources needed, the expected lifetime of the high-risk AI system and any necessary maintenance and care measures, including their frequency, to ensure the proper functioning of that AI system, including as regards software updates?
      `the instructions for use contain where relevant, a description of the mechanisms included within the high-risk AI system that allows deployers to properly collect, store and interpret the logs in accordance with Article 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where it is relevant, do the instructions for use contain a description of the mechanisms included within the high-risk AI system that allow deployers to properly collect, store and interpret the logs in accordance with Article 12? Answer yes if it is not relevant.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 13(3), as a provider of an AI system, do the instructions for use of my high-risk AI system contain at least the information the paragraph lists` IS
    `Art 13(3) the instructions for use contain at least the following information` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the instructions for use contain the identity and the contact details of the provider and, where applicable, of its authorised representative` `the instructions for use contain the characteristics, capabilities and limitations of performance of the high-risk AI system` `the instructions for use contain its intended purpose` `the instructions for use contain the level of accuracy, including its metrics, robustness and cybersecurity referred to in Article 15 against which the high-risk AI system has been tested and validated and which can be expected, and any known and foreseeable circumstances that may have an impact on that expected level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity` `the instructions for use contain any known or foreseeable circumstance, related to the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, which may lead to risks to the health and safety or fundamental rights referred to in Article 9(2)` `the instructions for use contain where applicable, the technical capabilities and characteristics of the high-risk AI system to provide information that is relevant to explain its output` `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, its performance regarding specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used` `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, specifications for the input data, or any other relevant information in terms of the training, validation and testing data sets used, taking into account the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` `the instructions for use contain where applicable, information to enable deployers to interpret the output of the high-risk AI system and use it appropriately` `the instructions for use contain the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance which have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment, if any` `the instructions for use contain the human oversight measures referred to in Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of the high-risk AI systems by the deployers` `the instructions for use contain the computational and hardware resources needed, the expected lifetime of the high-risk AI system and any necessary maintenance and care measures, including their frequency, to ensure the proper functioning of that AI system, including as regards software updates` `the instructions for use contain where relevant, a description of the mechanisms included within the high-risk AI system that allows deployers to properly collect, store and interpret the logs in accordance with Article 12`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

§ `Under Article 14: human oversight`

@export Under Article 14(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system designed and developed in such a way, including with appropriate human-machine interface tools, that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which it is in use?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which it is in use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which it is in use?
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed with appropriate human-machine interface tools` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the high-risk AI system is designed and developed with appropriate human-machine interface tools?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 14(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system designed and developed in such a way, including with appropriate human-machine interface tools, that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which it is in use` IS
    `Art 14(1) the high-risk AI system is designed and developed so that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way that it can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which it is in use` `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed with appropriate human-machine interface tools`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 14(2), as a provider of an AI system, does the human oversight of my high-risk AI system aim to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when it is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `human oversight aims to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, in particular where such risks persist despite the application of other requirements set out in this Section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that human oversight aims to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, in particular where such risks persist despite the application of other requirements set out in this Section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 14(2), as a provider of an AI system, does the human oversight of my high-risk AI system aim to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when it is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse` IS
    `Art 14(2) human oversight aims to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `human oversight aims to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, in particular where such risks persist despite the application of other requirements set out in this Section`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 14(3), as a provider of an AI system, are the oversight measures for my high-risk AI system commensurate with its risks, level of autonomy and context of use, and ensured through measures built into the system by me, or measures I identified for the deployer to implement, or both?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the oversight measures are commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the oversight measures are commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use of the high-risk AI system?
      `measures identified and, when technically feasible, built into the high-risk AI system by the provider before it is placed on the market or put into service ensure the oversight` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there measures identified by the provider before the placing on the market or putting into service and, when technically feasible, built into the high-risk AI system, through which the oversight is ensured?
      `measures identified by the provider before placing the high-risk AI system on the market or putting it into service, and that are appropriate to be implemented by the deployer, ensure the oversight` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that measures identified by the provider before placing the high-risk AI system on the market or putting it into service, and that are appropriate to be implemented by the deployer, ensure the oversight?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 14(3), as a provider of an AI system, are the oversight measures for my high-risk AI system commensurate with its risks, level of autonomy and context of use, and ensured through measures built into the system by me, or measures I identified for the deployer to implement, or both` IS
    `Art 14(3) the oversight measures are commensurate with the risks and ensured through one or both types of measures` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the oversight measures are commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use of the high-risk AI system` `measures identified and, when technically feasible, built into the high-risk AI system by the provider before it is placed on the market or put into service ensure the oversight` `measures identified by the provider before placing the high-risk AI system on the market or putting it into service, and that are appropriate to be implemented by the deployer, ensure the oversight`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 14(4), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system provided to the deployer in such a way that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to do each of the five things the paragraph lists?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the high-risk AI system is provided to the deployer in such a way that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to do the things listed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the high-risk AI system provided to the deployer in such a way that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to do the things the next five questions list?
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to properly understand the relevant capacities and limitations of the high-risk AI system and to duly monitor its operation, including in view of detecting and addressing anomalies, dysfunctions and unexpected performance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they enabled to properly understand the relevant capacities and limitations of the high-risk AI system and to duly monitor its operation, including in view of detecting and addressing anomalies, dysfunctions and unexpected performance? Answer yes if that is not appropriate and proportionate.
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to remain aware of the possible tendency of automatically relying or over-relying on the output produced by the high-risk AI system (automation bias)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they enabled to remain aware of the possible tendency of automatically relying or over-relying on the output produced by the high-risk AI system (automation bias)? Answer yes if that is not appropriate and proportionate.
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to correctly interpret the output of the high-risk AI system, taking into account, for example, the interpretation tools and methods available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they enabled to correctly interpret the output of the high-risk AI system, taking into account, for example, the interpretation tools and methods available? Answer yes if that is not appropriate and proportionate.
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to decide, in any particular situation, not to use the high-risk AI system or to otherwise disregard, override or reverse its output` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they enabled to decide, in any particular situation, not to use the high-risk AI system or to otherwise disregard, override or reverse its output? Answer yes if that is not appropriate and proportionate.
      `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to intervene in the operation of the high-risk AI system or interrupt it through a 'stop' button or a similar procedure that allows the system to come to a halt in a safe state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they enabled to intervene in the operation of the high-risk AI system or interrupt it through a 'stop' button or a similar procedure that allows the system to come to a halt in a safe state? Answer yes if that is not appropriate and proportionate.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 14(4), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system provided to the deployer in such a way that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to do each of the five things the paragraph lists` IS
    `Art 14(4) the high-risk AI system is provided to the deployer so that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled to do the following` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the high-risk AI system is provided to the deployer in such a way that the natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to do the things listed` `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to properly understand the relevant capacities and limitations of the high-risk AI system and to duly monitor its operation, including in view of detecting and addressing anomalies, dysfunctions and unexpected performance` `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to remain aware of the possible tendency of automatically relying or over-relying on the output produced by the high-risk AI system (automation bias)` `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to correctly interpret the output of the high-risk AI system, taking into account, for example, the interpretation tools and methods available` `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to decide, in any particular situation, not to use the high-risk AI system or to otherwise disregard, override or reverse its output` `the natural persons are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate, to intervene in the operation of the high-risk AI system or interrupt it through a 'stop' button or a similar procedure that allows the system to come to a halt in a safe state`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 14(5), as a provider of an AI system, in the first subparagraph, if my high-risk AI system is a system referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III, are the oversight measures such as to ensure that no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the high-risk AI system one referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III (a remote biometric identification system, not one used only for biometric verification to confirm that a specific natural person is who they claim to be)?
      `the measures referred to in paragraph 3 are such as to ensure that, in addition, no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your AI system, is it the case that the measures referred to in paragraph 3 are such as to ensure that, in addition, no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 14(5), as a provider of an AI system, in the first subparagraph, if my high-risk AI system is a system referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III, are the oversight measures such as to ensure that no action or decision is taken by the deployer on the basis of the identification resulting from the system unless that identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority` IS
