-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat provider from part P5 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P5-seat-provider: the questions a provider of an AI system (in particular of a high-risk AI system) can ask of Articles 40 to 49 and Annexes V, VI, VIII and IX. A seat module calls layer 1 and restates no rule.
-- A provider holds this role (the keel's Art 3(3) role question is not asked again here).

§ `Article 40: does the group apply?`

-- The applicability question: Article 113 as amended dates Chapter III Section 5 (Articles 40 to 49) and the Annexes of this part by its second paragraph (the General group; keel fork F-113-groups, assumed).
@export Under Article 40, as a provider of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 40, as a provider of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

§ `Under Article 40(1)`

-- Is my high-risk AI system presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2? (layer 1: Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set...)
@export Under Article 40(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? It matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I: Article 2(2) then limits which provisions of the Regulation apply to it. Answer no if it is not, or if you do not know.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Under Article 2(2) this matters only for Articles 57 to 59, so it does not change the answer to this question. Answer no if you do not know.
      `the standard is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the standard is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012? Answer yes or no.
      `the high-risk AI system is in conformity with the harmonised standard or parts thereof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the high-risk AI system is in conformity with the harmonised standard or parts thereof? Answer yes or no.
      `the references of the harmonised standard have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the references of the harmonised standard have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012? Answer yes or no.
      `the harmonised standard covers the requirement set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the harmonised standard covers the requirement set out in Section 2? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 40(1), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` IS
    `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the standard is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` `the high-risk AI system is in conformity with the harmonised standard or parts thereof` `the references of the harmonised standard have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` `the harmonised standard covers the requirement set out in Section 2`

