GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? It matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I: Article 2(2) then limits which provisions of the Regulation apply to it. Answer no if it is not, or if you do not know.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Under Article 2(2) this matters only for Articles 57 to 59, so it does not change the answer to this question. Answer no if you do not know.
      `the high-risk AI system falls within the scope of Regulation (EU) 2024/2847` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the high-risk AI system falls within the scope of Regulation (EU) 2024/2847? Answer yes or no.
      `the conditions laid down in Article 12(1) of Regulation (EU) 2024/2847 are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the conditions laid down in Article 12(1) of Regulation (EU) 2024/2847 are fulfilled? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 42(3), as a provider of an AI system, is my high-risk AI system deemed to comply with the cybersecurity requirement set out in Article 15` IS
    `Art 42(3) the high-risk AI system is deemed to comply with the cybersecurity requirement set out in Article 15` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the high-risk AI system falls within the scope of Regulation (EU) 2024/2847` `the conditions laid down in Article 12(1) of Regulation (EU) 2024/2847 are fulfilled`

§ `Under Article 43(1)`

-- Which conformity assessment procedure must I follow? (layer 1: Art 43(1) the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow)
@export Under Article 43(1), as a provider of an AI system, which conformity assessment procedure must I follow?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? It matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I: Article 2(2) then limits which provisions of the Regulation apply to it. Answer no if it is not, or if you do not know.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Under Article 2(2) this matters only for Articles 57 to 59, so it does not change the answer to this question. Answer no if you do not know.
      `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which point of Annex III is the high-risk AI system listed? Give the number of the point, from 1 to 8.
      `the provider has applied harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the provider has applied harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41? Answer yes or no.
      `harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 do not exist, and common specifications referred to in Article 41 are not available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 do not exist, and common specifications referred to in Article 41 are not available? Answer yes or no.
      `the provider has not applied, or has applied only part of, the harmonised standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the provider has not applied, or has applied only part of, the harmonised standard? Answer yes or no.
      `the common specifications referred to in point (a) exist, but the provider has not applied them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the common specifications referred to in point (a) exist, but the provider has not applied them? Answer yes or no.
      `one or more of the harmonised standards referred to in point (a) has been published with a restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: one or more of the harmonised standards referred to in point (a) has been published with a restriction? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 43 procedure`
DECIDE `Under Article 43(1), as a provider of an AI system, which conformity assessment procedure must I follow` IS
    `Art 43(1) the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` `the provider has applied harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41` `harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 do not exist, and common specifications referred to in Article 41 are not available` `the provider has not applied, or has applied only part of, the harmonised standard` `the common specifications referred to in point (a) exist, but the provider has not applied them` `one or more of the harmonised standards referred to in point (a) has been published with a restriction`

-- Which body carries out the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII? (layer 1: Art 43(1) the body that carries out the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII)
@export Under Article 43(1), as a provider of an AI system, which body carries out the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? It matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I: Article 2(2) then limits which provisions of the Regulation apply to it. Answer no if it is not, or if you do not know.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Under Article 2(2) this matters only for Articles 57 to 59, so it does not change the answer to this question. Answer no if you do not know.
      `the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII is carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII is carried out? Answer yes or no.
      `the high-risk AI system is intended to be put into service by law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities or by Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the high-risk AI system is intended to be put into service by law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities or by Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 43(1) body`
DECIDE `Under Article 43(1), as a provider of an AI system, which body carries out the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII` IS
    `Art 43(1) the body that carries out the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII is carried out` `the high-risk AI system is intended to be put into service by law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities or by Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies`

