-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat provider from part P7 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P7-seat-provider: THE SEAT LAYER for a provider of an AI system (or a prospective provider), over the layer-1 modules of Articles 57 to 71 of
-- the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: the provider. This layer phrases the rules already encoded in P7-sandboxes, P7-testing, P7-sme, P7-governance and P7-database as the questions a provider
-- would ask about its own AI system: may I use the sandbox exit report, is my testing in real world conditions allowed, have I obtained informed consent, may I use
-- the simplified quality management system, what the EU database holds about my system. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls one layer-1 function.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, a number, or one of the keel's own choices, each with an @desc. The date asked comes first.
-- Seam inputs: S1 (the route by which the AI system is high-risk, the core's own choice), S14 (Article 2(2): the route, whether the products are covered by the Section B legislation and whether the requirements are integrated in it, passed to the keel's `Art 2(2)`), S12 (enterprise size, asked as a yes/no).
-- Articles 57 to 63 and 71 are in the provision group `General` (from 2 August 2026); Articles 64 to 70 are in the group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` (from 2 August 2025):
-- each has one applicability question. Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled).
-- The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.
-- Conditions that the text lists in points (for example Article 59(1)(a) to (j)) are asked as one yes/no each, worded as the point is; the question does not judge them for the provider.

§ `Under Article 57: the group General and the AI regulatory sandboxes`

-- Chapter VI (Articles 57 to 63) and Chapter VIII (Article 71) apply from 2 August 2026. A provider is in a sandbox only if it applied to one; the questions about the sandbox arise only then.

-- The applicability question for the provision group `General` that Article 57 opens in this part's range: it asks only the date, and passes the core's constants for the route, the placement date and the change.
@export Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- The role question. Article 3(3) defines the provider: whoever develops, or has developed, an AI system or general-purpose AI model and places it on the market or puts the AI system into service under its own name or trademark. The other questions of this seat assume you hold this role.
@export Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, am I a provider of an AI system?
GIVEN `the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you develop an AI system or a general-purpose AI model?
      `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed for you?
      `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you place it on the market, or put the AI system into service?
      `the party does so under its own name or trademark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do so under your own name or trademark?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, am I a provider of an AI system` IS
    `Art 3(3) the party is a provider` `the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed` `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service` `the party does so under its own name or trademark`

-- Article 57(7). A provider that took part in a sandbox may use the documentation it received to show compliance in the conformity assessment or in market surveillance.
@export Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, may I use the written proof and the exit report of the AI regulatory sandbox to demonstrate compliance with the Regulation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products to which your AI system relates covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation (the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I that covers the products)?
      `the documentation is the written proof or the exit report of the sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the documentation the written proof of the activities carried out in the sandbox, or the exit report, given to you by the national competent authority?
      `the provider uses it to demonstrate compliance with this Regulation through the conformity assessment process or relevant market surveillance activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you using it to demonstrate compliance with the Regulation through the conformity assessment process or in relevant market surveillance activities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, may I use the written proof and the exit report of the AI regulatory sandbox to demonstrate compliance with the Regulation` IS
    `Art 57(7) the provider may use the written proof and the exit report to demonstrate compliance` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the documentation is the written proof or the exit report of the sandbox` `the provider uses it to demonstrate compliance with this Regulation through the conformity assessment process or relevant market surveillance activities`

-- Article 57(12), first sentence. Taking part in a sandbox does not take the liability away.
@export Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, do I remain liable under applicable Union and national liability law for damage inflicted on third parties by my experimentation in the sandbox?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products to which your AI system relates covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation (the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I that covers the products)?
      `damage was inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that damage was inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, do I remain liable under applicable Union and national liability law for damage inflicted on third parties by my experimentation in the sandbox` IS
    `Art 57(12) the provider remains liable under applicable Union and national liability law for damage inflicted on third parties` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `damage was inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox`

-- Article 57(12), second sentence. No administrative fine is imposed for infringements of the Regulation if the participant observes the specific plan and the terms and follows the guidance in good faith.
@export Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, is the imposition of administrative fines for infringements of this Regulation on me barred while I follow the sandbox plan and the authority's guidance in good faith?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products to which your AI system relates covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation (the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I that covers the products)?
      `the prospective provider observes the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the prospective provider observes the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation? Answer yes or no.
      `the prospective provider follows in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the prospective provider follows in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a provider of an AI system, is the imposition of administrative fines for infringements of this Regulation on me barred while I follow the sandbox plan and the authority's guidance in good faith` IS
    `Art 57(12) the imposition of administrative fines for infringements of this Regulation on the prospective provider is barred` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the prospective provider observes the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation` `the prospective provider follows in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority`


§ `Under Article 58: the arrangements of the sandboxes`

