§ `Under Article 59: personal data in the sandbox`

-- Article 59(1): lawfully collected personal data may be processed in the sandbox solely for developing, training and testing certain AI systems, when all ten conditions of points (a) to (j) are met.
@export Under Article 59, as a provider of an AI system, may personal data lawfully collected for other purposes be processed in the AI regulatory sandbox for developing, training and testing my AI system?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products to which your AI system relates covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation (the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I that covers the products)?
      `the personal data were lawfully collected for other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the personal data lawfully collected for other purposes?
      `the processing is solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing the AI system in the sandbox` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing your AI system in the sandbox?
      `the condition of point (a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system developed for safeguarding substantial public interest by a public authority or another natural or legal person, in one of the areas the point lists (public safety and health, the environment, energy sustainability, transport and critical infrastructure, public administration)?
      `the condition of point (b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the data processed necessary for complying with one or more of the requirements of Chapter III, Section 2, where those requirements cannot effectively be fulfilled by processing anonymised, synthetic or other non-personal data?
      `the condition of point (c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there effective monitoring mechanisms to identify high risks to the rights and freedoms of the data subjects during the sandbox experimentation, and response mechanisms to mitigate them promptly and, where necessary, stop the processing?
      `the condition of point (d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the personal data in a functionally separate, isolated and protected data processing environment under your control, with access limited to authorised persons?
      `the condition of point (e) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you share the originally collected data further only in accordance with Union data protection law, and is no personal data created in the sandbox shared outside it?
      `the condition of point (f) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the processing neither lead to measures or decisions affecting the data subjects nor affect the application of their rights under Union law on the protection of personal data?
      `the condition of point (g) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the personal data protected by appropriate technical and organisational measures and deleted once your participation has terminated or the data has reached the end of its retention period?
      `the condition of point (h) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the logs of the processing kept for the duration of your participation in the sandbox, unless Union or national law provides otherwise?
      `the condition of point (i) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a complete and detailed description of the process and rationale behind the training, testing and validation of the AI system kept together with the testing results as part of the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV?
      `the condition of point (j) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a short summary of the AI project, its objectives and expected results published on the website of the competent authorities (sensitive operational data of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities need not be included)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 59, as a provider of an AI system, may personal data lawfully collected for other purposes be processed in the AI regulatory sandbox for developing, training and testing my AI system` IS
    `Art 59(1) the personal data may be processed in the AI regulatory sandbox for developing, training and testing the AI system` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the personal data were lawfully collected for other purposes` `the processing is solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing the AI system in the sandbox` `the conditions of points (a) to (j) are each met`
    WHERE
        `the conditions of points (a) to (j) are each met` MEANS LIST `the condition of point (a) is met`, `the condition of point (b) is met`, `the condition of point (c) is met`, `the condition of point (d) is met`, `the condition of point (e) is met`, `the condition of point (f) is met`, `the condition of point (g) is met`, `the condition of point (h) is met`, `the condition of point (i) is met`, `the condition of point (j) is met`


§ `Under Article 60: testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes`

-- Article 60(1). As amended, a high-risk system listed in Annex III, or covered by Section A of Annex I, may be tested in real world conditions in accordance with Article 60 and the real-world testing plan; a system under Section B of Annex I is for Article 60a.
@export Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, may I conduct testing of my high-risk AI system in real world conditions outside an AI regulatory sandbox?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products to which your AI system relates covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation (the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I that covers the products)?
      `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I?
      `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the testing conducted in accordance with Article 60 and the real-world testing plan?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, may I conduct testing of my high-risk AI system in real world conditions outside an AI regulatory sandbox` IS
    `Art 60(1) the provider may conduct testing in real world conditions outside the sandboxes` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the AI system is covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` `the testing is conducted in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan`

-- Article 60(4)(b): approval, or tacit approval where the authority gives no answer within 30 days and national law provides for tacit approval; where it does not, the testing remains subject to an authorisation.
@export Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, has the market surveillance authority approved my testing and my real-world testing plan, expressly or by tacit approval?
GIVEN `the market surveillance authority has approved the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan, expressly or by an authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the market surveillance authority expressly approved the testing and the plan, or granted an authorisation?
      `the market surveillance authority has provided an answer within 30 days of the submission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the authority give you an answer within 30 days of your submission of the plan?
      `national law provides for a tacit approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the national law of the Member State where the testing is to be conducted provide for tacit approval?
      `the date on which the plan was submitted` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you submit the real-world testing plan to the market surveillance authority?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, has the market surveillance authority approved my testing and my real-world testing plan, expressly or by tacit approval` IS
    `Art 60(4)(b) the market surveillance authority has approved the testing and the plan` `the market surveillance authority has approved the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan, expressly or by an authorisation` `the market surveillance authority has provided an answer within 30 days of the submission` `national law provides for a tacit approval` `the date on which the plan was submitted` `the date asked`

-- Article 60(4)(c): one of three registrations, by the kind of system: Article 71(4) with Annex IX; the secure non-public section under Article 49(4)(d) (Annex III points 1, 6, 7 in law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control); Article 49(5) (Annex III point 2).
@export Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, have I registered my testing in real world conditions as the Regulation requires?
GIVEN `the AI system is referred to in points 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI system is referred to in points 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management? Answer yes or no.
      `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III? Answer yes or no.
      `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 71(4) with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified in Annex IX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 71(4) with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified in Annex IX? Answer yes or no.
      `the testing has been registered in the secure non-public section of the EU database according to Article 49(4), point (d), with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified therein` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing has been registered in the secure non-public section of the EU database according to Article 49(4), point (d), with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified therein? Answer yes or no.
      `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 49(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 49(5)? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, have I registered my testing in real world conditions as the Regulation requires` IS
    `Art 60(4)(c) the testing in real world conditions has been registered as the text requires` `the AI system is referred to in points 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management` `the AI system is referred to in point 2 of Annex III` `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 71(4) with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified in Annex IX` `the testing has been registered in the secure non-public section of the EU database according to Article 49(4), point (d), with a Union-wide unique single identification number and with the information specified therein` `the testing has been registered in accordance with Article 49(5)`

-- Article 60(4)(f): not longer than necessary and in any case not longer than six months, which may be extended for a further six months on prior notification with an explanation.
@export Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, does my testing in real world conditions stay within the time the Regulation allows?
GIVEN `the testing does not last longer than necessary to achieve its objectives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing does not last longer than necessary to achieve its objectives? Answer yes or no.
      `the date on which the testing began` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date on which the testing began?
      `the date on which the testing ended or is asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the date on which the testing ended or is asked about?
      `the testing has been extended for an additional period of six months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing has been extended for an additional period of six months? Answer yes or no.
      `the provider or prospective provider notified the market surveillance authority beforehand, with an explanation of the need for the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider or prospective provider notified the market surveillance authority beforehand, with an explanation of the need for the extension? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, does my testing in real world conditions stay within the time the Regulation allows` IS
    `Art 60(4)(f) the testing does not last longer than the text allows` `the testing does not last longer than necessary to achieve its objectives` `the date on which the testing began` `the date on which the testing ended or is asked about` `the testing has been extended for an additional period of six months` `the provider or prospective provider notified the market surveillance authority beforehand, with an explanation of the need for the extension`

-- Article 60(4)(d). The text says "legal representative"; it is read as the authorised representative of Article 3(5) (fork F-60-4-d).
@export Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, am I established in the Union, or have I appointed a legal representative established in the Union, as the testing requires?
GIVEN `the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing is established in the Union? Answer yes or no.
      `the provider or prospective provider has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider or prospective provider has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, am I established in the Union, or have I appointed a legal representative established in the Union, as the testing requires` IS
    `Art 60(4)(d) the provider is established in the Union or has appointed a legal representative established in the Union` `the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing is established in the Union` `the provider or prospective provider has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union`

-- Article 60(4)(h).
@export Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, if I organise the testing with deployers or prospective deployers, have they been informed of all relevant aspects and given the instructions for use, and have we concluded an agreement on roles and responsibilities?
GIVEN `the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers? Answer yes or no.
      `the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate? Answer yes or no.
      `the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13? Answer yes or no.
      `the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, if I organise the testing with deployers or prospective deployers, have they been informed of all relevant aspects and given the instructions for use, and have we concluded an agreement on roles and responsibilities` IS
    `Art 60(4)(h) the deployers taking part have been informed and an agreement concluded` `the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` `the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate` `the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13` `the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities`

-- Article 60(4): testing may be conducted only where all eleven conditions (a) to (k) are met.
@export Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, are all the conditions for conducting my testing in real world conditions met?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the products to which your AI system relates covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation (the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I that covers the products)?
      `the condition of point (a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you drawn up a real-world testing plan and submitted it to the market surveillance authority in the Member State where the testing is to be conducted?
      `the condition of point (b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the market surveillance authority approved the testing and the plan (expressly, tacitly after 30 days where national law provides, or by an authorisation)?
      `the condition of point (c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you registered the testing as the Regulation requires for your kind of system (Article 71(4) and Annex IX, the secure section under Article 49(4)(d), or Article 49(5))?
      `the condition of point (d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you established in the Union, or have you appointed a legal representative established in the Union?
      `the condition of point (e) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the data collected for the testing transferred to third countries only with appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law?
      `the condition of point (f) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the testing last no longer than necessary and in any case no longer than six months, extended for at most six more months on prior notification with an explanation?
      `the condition of point (g) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are subjects who belong to vulnerable groups due to age or disability appropriately protected?
      `the condition of point (h) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you organise the testing with deployers or prospective deployers: have they been informed of all relevant aspects and given the instructions for use, and have you concluded an agreement on roles and responsibilities?
      `the condition of point (i) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the subjects given informed consent in accordance with Article 61 (or, in law enforcement where seeking consent would prevent the testing, are there no negative effects and is the data deleted afterwards)?
      `the condition of point (j) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the testing effectively overseen by you and by the deployers through suitably qualified persons with the necessary capacity, training and authority?
      `the condition of point (k) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system be effectively reversed and disregarded?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a provider of an AI system, are all the conditions for conducting my testing in real world conditions met` IS
    `Art 60(4) the conditions for conducting the testing in real world conditions are met` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the condition of point (a) is met` `the condition of point (b) is met` `the condition of point (c) is met` `the condition of point (d) is met` `the condition of point (e) is met` `the condition of point (f) is met` `the condition of point (g) is met` `the condition of point (h) is met` `the condition of point (i) is met` `the condition of point (j) is met` `the condition of point (k) is met`

